.TH QUADRF 1 "August 2026" "QuadRF" "QuadRF"
.SH NAME
quadrf \- inspect and configure a QuadRF appliance
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B quadrf
.RI [ command ]
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B quadrf
reports the state of the appliance and re-applies the site configuration held
in
.IR /etc/quadrf/quadrf.conf .
With no command it behaves as
.BR "quadrf status" .
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Print each installed QuadRF service with its enabled and active state, whether
the CSI and DSI drivers are loaded, the SoapySDR devices that can be found, and
the addresses on wlan0, eth0 and usb0 (USB only while a gadget host is
attached). A pending reboot is reported last.
.TP
.B apply
Run every configuration hook in
.I /usr/lib/quadrf/apply.d
in order, then reload systemd. Each installed package contributes one hook, so
this re-applies the firmware block, the service account drop-ins, the generated
network configuration and the desktop layout. Safe to repeat. Needs root.
.TP
.B packages
List the installed quadrf-* packages and their versions.
.TP
.BI "tls import " directory
Install
.I fullchain.pem
and
.I privkey.pem
from
.I directory
into
.I /etc/quadrf/tls
and reload nginx. A Let's Encrypt live directory can be given directly. Needs
root.
.TP
.B tls self-signed
Discard the installed certificate and regenerate the self-signed placeholder
for the configured domain. Needs root.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/quadrf/quadrf.conf
Site configuration. See
.BR quadrf.conf (5).
.TP
.I /usr/lib/quadrf/apply.d/
Configuration hooks, one per installed package.
.TP
.I /var/lib/quadrf/reboot-required
Written when a change needs a restart to take effect. Cleared on the next
boot by
.BR quadrf-reboot-clear.service .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR quadrf.conf (5),
.BR quadrf-jtag (1),
.BR quadrf-load (8)
